Web Inspector on Kosmos (docs/webkit.html, Developer mode, 15 November
2026). The UI process's platform half is Kosmos's own
(UIProcess/Inspector/kosmos/WebInspectorUIProxyKosmos.cpp), so the stubs
for ports without one are left out; and the front end's localized
strings are found beside its own page, in the folder on the disk it was
loaded from; and its folder is one the UI process takes the web
process to read already, as Safari's port does for its own bundle, so a
page of the inspector's is never asked for a sandbox extension - which
WebKit asserts it never needs.

